Thanks that works much better! From the plot, it looks like the neuron objects (both transformed and non transformed) are a lot bigger and way out of range from the bounding box. Does this mean that my original average and CMTK registrations were done incorrectly? In order to make the average, I picked the brain with the largest stack size and registered all other brains to that one (using munger -awr in the terminal). I then used the cmtk function average_brains to create a simple average of all those resulting warped brain images  (which I assumed were in the folder 'reformatted') and then registered each original brain to the newly created average. The neuron filament objects which I segmented for each brain in Imaris were then exported out as swc files and imported into r where I was able to transform them by the registration .list files generated by the last registration. I had assumed that I had been previously doing everything correctly but now I am unsure as to how I should proceed. You you have any further tips on the best way to trouble shoot this situation and figure out where I went wrong based on my methods so far?

Max

